%% DESIGNED, nothing built (docs/architecture/pod-reaper.md, with its updates to 2026-10-30). Pods that restart in place leave no hourly Failed pods, so what it is wanted for now is Failed
%% Jobs' pods, evicted pods of Deployments and old ReplicaSets, each recorded in the graph first. Until it is built, `just cluster-prune-failed`, by hand. N is not settled.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Sch as Scheduler
    participant Att as Attestation agent<br/>(the pod observer's role)
    participant K as Kubernetes API
    participant Graph as Neo4j
    participant Reaper as The Reaper
    participant Policy as PolicyActor
    participant VAP as ValidatingAdmissionPolicy

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Sch,VAP: DESIGNED: two agents, the one that sees and the one that may delete
    Sch-)Att: the inventory's schedule
    Att->>K: list what is finished, and its logs, with a namespaced Role
    Att->>Graph: the observable first: the pod, owner, exit code or eviction reason, the end of its log
    Att-)Reaper: the report. The Reaper checks published_by and the capability
    Reaper-)Att: when it restarts, ask for the current set
    Reaper->>Reaper: retention: the newest N, by signed configuration
    Reaper->>Policy: Action reap on Pod NAMESPACE/NAME, with phase, owner and age
    Policy-->>Reaper: Cedar's answer
    Reaper->>K: delete, with preconditions.uid
    K->>VAP: admitted only for a finished pod a Polar workload owns
    Reaper->>Graph: an edge to the reaping

    alt an old ReplicaSet
        Att->>Graph: the observable first: revision, digests, template hash, replaced at
        Reaper->>K: delete, keeping the newest N
        K->>VAP: refused for one with replicas, the current revision, or not of a Polar Deployment
    end
    end
